<article class="env-corollary" id="02VQ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02VQ">Corollary <span data-tag="02VQ">4.5.6.16</span>.</a> Let $q: X \rightarrow S$ be an isofibration of simplicial sets. Suppose we are given a morphism of simplicial sets $B \rightarrow S$ and a simplicial subset $A \subseteq B$. Then the restriction map $\theta : \operatorname{Fun}_{/S}( B, X ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}_{/S}(A, X)$ is an isofibration of $\infty $-categories. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      The morphism $\theta $ is a pullback of the isofibration $\operatorname{Fun}(B,X) \rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}(A,X) \times _{ \operatorname{Fun}(A,S) } \operatorname{Fun}(B,S)$ of Proposition <a data-tag="01G3" href="/tag/01G3">4.5.6.14</a>, and is therefore also an isofibration (Remark <a data-tag="01G1" href="/tag/01G1">4.5.6.11</a>). We conclude by observing that since $q$ is an inner fibration (Remark <a data-tag="01FX" href="/tag/01FX">4.5.6.7</a>), the simplicial sets $\operatorname{Fun}_{/S}(B,X)$ and $\operatorname{Fun}_{/S}(A,X)$ are $\infty $-categories (Proposition <a data-tag="01GQ" href="/tag/01GQ">4.1.4.6</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
